Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 00:36:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 061/106] media: input: pm8xxx-vibrator: fix the drv2 (extended
 voltage) shift direction

pmi632_regs uses a two-byte LDO voltage register pair (drv_offset=0x40
low byte, drv2_offset=0x41 with a 4-bit mask holding the upper bits of
a ~12-bit millivolt-scaled level, matching downstream's
qpnp-vibrator-ldo VSET_LB/VSET_LB+1 pair). Extracting the upper bits of
a value that can exceed 8 bits needs a RIGHT shift before masking into
the narrower drv2 register - the code does 'vib->level << drv2_shift'
instead, which for drv2_shift=8 always produces zero in the masked low
nibble (shifting left by 8 puts zero in bits 0-3 unconditionally),
capping the LDO's requested output voltage far below the 1504-3544mV
range the hardware needs to actually drive the motor.

Found and fixed while bringing up the vibrator on a Qualcomm SM7150
phone (surya) using this same register set. Not yet confirmed
sufficient on its own to produce physical vibration - see the surya
bring-up notes for the ongoing investigation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c b/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c
index 381b06473..94d51739f 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c
@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ static int pm8xxx_vib_set(struct pm8xxx_vib *vib, bool on)
 	vib->reg_vib_drv = val;
 
 	if (regs->drv2_mask) {
-		val = vib->level << regs->drv2_shift;
+		val = vib->level >> regs->drv2_shift;
 		rc = regmap_write_bits(vib->regmap, vib->drv2_addr,
 				regs->drv2_mask, on ? val : 0);
 		if (rc < 0)
